  "summary": "A precision measurement of the $K^{*0}$ meson yield is reported in Au+Au collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}} = 7.7,\\; 11.5,\\; 14.6,\\; 19.6,$ and $27~\\mathrm{GeV}$ using the high-statistics data sample collected by the STAR experiment during the Beam Energy Scan II (BES-II) program at RHIC. The transeverse momentum ($p_{T}$)-integrated yield ratios $(K^{*0} + \\overline{K^{*0}})/(K^{+} + K^{-})$ in central collisions show a suppression relative to peripheral collisions at the $(1.7\\text{-}3.6)\\,σ$ level, while a thermal model without final-stage rescattering overpredicts this ratio with a deviation…",
